  "why": "The paper explicitly targets detection of over-refusal (benign queries being refused) rather than discovering inputs that bypass safety safeguards to elicit harmful outputs. Its mutators and evaluation are intentionally designed to avoid producing harmful content, and the oracle (OR-JUDGE) is trained to identify safety-related refusals rather than to detect or exploit defenses. The authors contrast their goal with jailbreak work and do not present any experiments that attempt to circumvent or bypass deployed safeguards; thus the fuzzer is not designed to discover safeguard bypasses and does not demonstrate such bypasses empirically.",
